{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract benchmark [-h] [--profile {200mb,full,smoke,standard}] [--coverage COVERAGE]\n                            [--full-size]\n                            [--build {38,grch38,hg38,hs38,hs38d1,hs38d1v0,hs38dh,GRCh38,hs38DH,37,grch37,hg19,hg37,hs37,hs37d5,GRCh37,chm13,chm13v2,chm13v2.0,t2t,t2tv2,t2tv2.0,t2tv20,T2Tv20,T2Tv2,T2Tv2.0,CHM13,CHM13v2.0}]\n                            [-r REGION] [--keep-going] [--suite {core,heavy}]\n                            [--dataset {fake,real,real-1x,real-30x}] [--help-all]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --profile {200mb,full,smoke,standard}\n                        Benchmark size preset. smoke is chrM-only, standard is a scaled human-like genome, 200mb targets a ~200 MiB fake BAM, and full uses real chromosome lengths.\n  --coverage COVERAGE   Override generated BAM coverage for the selected profile.\n  --full-size           Use real chromosome lengths for the generated benchmark reference.\n  --build {38,grch38,hg38,hs38,hs38d1,hs38d1v0,hs38dh,GRCh38,hs38DH,37,grch37,hg19,hg37,hs37,hs37d5,GRCh37,chm13,chm13v2,chm13v2.0,t2t,t2tv2,t2tv2.0,t2tv20,T2Tv20,T2Tv2,T2Tv2.0,CHM13,CHM13v2.0}\n                        Generated reference naming/build convention.\n  -r, --region REGION   Optional region to benchmark for region-aware operations.\n  --keep-going          Continue independent benchmark steps after a failed step when possible.\n  --suite {core,heavy}  Benchmark operation coverage. core runs the lighter baseline suite.\n  --dataset {fake,real,real-1x,real-30x}\n                        Benchmark foundation data. fake generates synthetic data; real uses the release-backed mini genome zip; real-1x and real-30x cache public 1000 Genomes WGS references locally.\n  --help-all            Show this help with the advanced options too, and exit.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json,\n  --quiet, --debug, --config and the other global options are accepted before\n  or after the command; 'wgsextract --help' lists them all.\n\n6 advanced options not shown; 'wgsextract benchmark --help-all' lists them.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract benchmark --profile smoke\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  runs/<timestamp>/ under --outdir (default out/benchmark):\n  benchmark_report.md and benchmark_results.json (timings, tool versions) and\n  per-step logs.\n\nneeds:\n  no external tools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools, bgzip,\n  curl, samtools, tabix; hours for the full suite.\n",
